  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) is similar to quadrilateral \\(A'B'C'D'\\) (vertices correspond in order). Given \\(\\angle A=80^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=95^\\circ\\), and \\(\\angle C=100^\\circ\\), find the degree measure of \\(\\angle D'\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "85",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Corresponding angles of similar polygons are equal, so \\(\\angle D'=\\angle D\\). The sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral is \\(360^\\circ\\), so \\(\\angle D=360^\\circ-80^\\circ-95^\\circ-100^\\circ=85^\\circ\\).",
